.TH HOWLINUX 1 "2026-08-30" "howlinux 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
howlinux \- deterministic offline Linux knowledge search
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B howlinux
.RI [ options ] \ <query...>
.br
.B howlinux search
.RI [ options ] \ <query...>
.br
.B howlinux list | show \ <entry-id> | validate [path]
.SH DESCRIPTION
howlinux searches a local, human-maintained Knowledge Base and renders a
verified Markdown answer. It is offline, deterministic, and never executes
commands from a query or an answer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ,\ --help
Show help.
.TP
.BR -V ,\ --version
Show the version.
.TP
.BI --knowledge\ path
Use a specific Knowledge directory.
.TP
.BI --limit\ n
Return at most n suggestions.
.TP
.B --explain
Show query processing and ranking details.
.TP
.B --json
Use stable machine-readable JSON output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
howlinux "rename a folder"
howlinux --explain "what does chmod 755 mean"
howlinux --json "extract tar.gz"
howlinux validate knowledge
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I knowledge/
Default Knowledge Base in a source checkout.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/howlinux/knowledge/
Typical per-user installation location.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means success, 1 means no confident result or validation issue, 2 means
invalid arguments, and 3 means a configuration or Knowledge loading error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR cmake (1)
